ndencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"repository":{"id":95098170,"node_id":"MDEwOlJlcG9zaXRvcnk5NTA5ODE3MA==","name":"OpenMetrics","full_name":"prometheus/OpenMetrics","private":false,"owner":{"login":"prometheus","id":3380462,"node_id":"MDEyOk9yZ2FuaXphdGlvbjMzODA0NjI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3380462?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/prometheus","html_url":"https://github.com/prometheus","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prometheus/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prometheus/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prometheus/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prometheus/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prometheus/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prometheus/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prometheus/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prometheus/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prometheus/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"html_url":"https://github.com/prometheus/OpenMetrics","description":"Evolving the Prometheus exposition format into a standard.","fork":false,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prometheus/OpenMetrics","forks_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prometheus/OpenMetrics/forks","keys_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prometheus/OpenMetrics/keys{/key_id}","collaborators_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prometheus/OpenMetrics/collaborators{/collaborator}","teams_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prometheus/OpenMetrics/teams","hooks_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prometheus/OpenMetrics/hooks","issue_events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prometheus/OpenMetrics/issues/events{/number}","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prometheus/OpenMetrics/events","assignees_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prometheus/OpenMetrics/assignees{/user}","branches_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prometheus/OpenMetrics/branches{/branch}","tags_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prometheus/OpenMetrics/tags","blobs_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prometheus/OpenMetrics/git/blobs{/sha}","git_tags_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prometheus/OpenMetrics/git/tags{/sha}","git_refs_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prometheus/OpenMetrics/git/refs{/sha}","trees_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prometheus/OpenMetrics/git/trees{/sha}","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prometheus/OpenMetrics/statuses/{sha}","languages_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prometheus/OpenMetrics/languages","stargazers_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prometheus/OpenMetrics/stargazers","contributors_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prometheus/OpenMetrics/contributors","subscribers_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prometheus/OpenMetrics/subscribers","subscription_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prometheus/OpenMetrics/subscription","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prometheus/OpenMetrics/commits{/sha}","git_commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prometheus/OpenMetrics/git/commits{/sha}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prometheus/OpenMetrics/comments{/number}","issue_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prometheus/OpenMetrics/issues/comments{/number}","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prometheus/OpenMetrics/contents/{+path}","compare_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prometheus/OpenMetrics/compare/{base}...{head}","merges_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prometheus/OpenMetrics/merges","archive_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prometheus/OpenMetrics/{archive_format}{/ref}","downloads_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prometheus/OpenMetrics/downloads","issues_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prometheus/OpenMetrics/issues{/number}","pulls_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prometheus/OpenMetrics/pulls{/number}","milestones_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prometheus/OpenMetrics/milestones{/number}","notifications_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prometheus/OpenMetrics/notifications{?since,all,participating}","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prometheus/OpenMetrics/labels{/name}","releases_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prometheus/OpenMetrics/releases{/id}","deployments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prometheus/OpenMetrics/deployments","created_at":"2017-06-22T09:24:47Z","updated_at":"2026-03-08T23:35:27Z","pushed_at":"2025-06-02T13:06:29Z","git_url":"git://github.com/prometheus/OpenMetrics.git","ssh_url":"git@github.com:prometheus/OpenMetrics.git","clone_url":"https://github.com/prometheus/OpenMetrics.git","svn_url":"https://github.com/prometheus/OpenMetrics","homepage":"https://openmetrics.io","size":3689,"stargazers_count":2511,"watchers_count":2511,"language":"Go","has_issues":true,"has_projects":true,"has_downloads":true,"has_wiki":true,"has_pages":false,"has_discussions":false,"forks_count":177,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":37,"license":{"key":"apache-2.0","name":"Apache License 2.0","spdx_id":"Apache-2.0","url":"https://api.github.com/licenses/apache-2.0","node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTI="},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":true,"has_pull_requests":true,"pull_request_creation_policy":"all","topics":[],"visibility":"public","forks":177,"open_issues":37,"watchers":2511,"default_branch":"main","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"body":"This deserves its own proposal, but i'll outline the broad idea here start the discussion and gather high-level feedback.\r\n\r\n### Idea\r\n\r\nThe idea is that we could use complex values for fixed bucket histograms, summaries, and counters, similar to what we [plan to do for native histograms](https://github.com/prometheus/proposals/pull/32). In OM 1.0 and in the Prometheus text format, those types are represented using multiple series with suffixes and special labels (e.g. `_bucket` suffix, or the `le` label for histograms). Counters are included here because they have a \"total\" and a \"start time\".\r\n\r\n### Advantages\r\n\r\n* Solves https://github.com/prometheus/prometheus/issues/6541 by supporting the created timestamp in the value.\r\n* Prevents collisions between suffixed series names and unsuffixed series names of a different type.\r\n    * E.g. `histogram: my_metric` vs `gauge: my_metric_bucket`\r\n* Removes PromQL differences between querying native and classic histograms: https://grafana.com/docs/mimir/latest/visualize/native-histograms/#query-your-histograms-count-or-sum (couldn't find Prometheus documentation)\r\n* Names in PromQL queries always match names defined in the application.\r\n    * This is helpful for metrics defined in other metric libraries, such as OpenTelemetry, where users don't expect suffixes.\r\n\r\n### Disadvantages\r\n\r\n* Breaks existing user expectations and queries. Suffixes are very deeply embedded in the Prometheus ecosystem, and this would be a large change for many users.\r\n* PromQL queries become more complicated because accessing fields requires functions.\r\n    * E.g. `sum(request_duration_seconds_count)` -> `histogram_count(sum(request_duration_seconds))`.\r\n    * This would happen anyways if the user migrates to native histograms.\r\n* Little benefit for summaries and histograms, as we expect/recommend users adopt native histograms anyways.\r\n* Is there a text format representation that is readable AND easy to generate AND efficient enough to parse, for such a model?\r\n* It would make OM 2.0 text significantly different to 1.0 and Prometheus text, so some education and big change in parsers/generators would be needed. Not a blocker, but something to keep in mind as a con.\r\n\r\n### Alternatives\r\n\r\nWe could only use a complex value for counters, to support the start time in addition to the value.  For fixed-bucket histograms and summaries, keep the existing suffixes and labels, but use the \"complex counter\" value for cumulative series.  For users that have migrated from summaries and fixed-bucket histograms to native histograms, this has most of the advantages of the above, without many of the disadvantages for users using summaries or fixed-bucket histograms.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prometheus/OpenMetrics/issues/283/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prometheus/OpenMetrics/issues/283/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prometheus/prometheus/issues/comments/3252570263","html_url":"https://github.com/prometheus/prometheus/issues/17140#issuecomment-3252570263","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prometheus/prometheus/issues/17140","id":3252570263,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAGhaic7B3kiX","user":{"login":"madaraszg-tulip","id":144027382,"node_id":"U_kgDOCJWu9g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/144027382?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/madaraszg-tulip","html_url":"https://github.com/madaraszg-tulip","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/madaraszg-tulip/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/madaraszg-tulip/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/madaraszg-tulip/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/madaraszg-tulip/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/madaraszg-tulip/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/madaraszg-tulip/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/madaraszg-tulip/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/madaraszg-tulip/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/madaraszg-tulip/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-04T08:52:18Z","updated_at":"2025-09-04T08:52:18Z","body":"I configured nhcb conversion again, picked an error from mimir-distributor:\n\n```\nts=2025-09-04T08:35:56.872123138Z caller=push.go:251 level=error user=anonymous traceID=215b8da78db644f3df043af2a641d1b4 msg=\"detected an error while ingesting Prometheus remote-write request (the request may have been partially ingested)\" httpCode=400 err=\"send data to ingesters: failed pushing to ingester mimir-testing-ingester-zone-b-2: user=anonymous: err: custom buckets: only 0 custom bounds defined which is insufficient to cover total span length of 8: histogram custom bounds are too few. timestamp=2025-09-04T08:35:56.233Z, series=[{__name__ loki_cache_request_duration_seconds} {cluster global-testing} {container ingester} {endpoint http-metrics} {garden global} {instance 10.19.246.52:3100} {job loki-testing/ingester-zone-a-headless} {method chunksmemcache.fetch} {name chunksmemcache} {namespace loki-testing} {pod loki-testing-ingester-zone-a-1} {prometheus monitoring-testing/clustermon-global-testing-prometheus} {prometheus_replica prometheus-clustermon-global-testing-prometheus-0} {service loki-testing-ingester-zone-a-headless} {status_code 200}] (err-mimir-native-histogram-custom-buckets-mismatch) (sampled 1/10)\" insight=true   \n```\n\nI then checked if I have any series for this metric name in mimir:\n\n`histogram_avg(rate(loki_cache_request_duration_seconds[$__rate_interval]))`\n\nNo results at all. \n\nAnd then I got the metrics directly from the pod using curl, and got the following: \n\n```\nloki_cache_request_duration_seconds_bucket{method=\"chunksmemcache.fetch\",name=\"chunksmemcache\",status_code=\"200\",le=\"6.4e-05\"} 0\nloki_cache_request_duration_seconds_bucket{method=\"chunksmemcache.fetch\",name=\"chunksmemcache\",status_code=\"200\",le=\"0.000256\"} 0\nloki_cache_request_du